WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.308
NARRATOR: An educational video should begin
with material a course owner trusts.

2
00:00:04.308 --> 00:00:09.002
NARRATOR: One-Click AI Video Generator turns
an approved topic, paper, or source pack

3
00:00:09.002 --> 00:00:12.522
NARRATOR: document, or storyboard into the
same structured episode plan.

4
00:00:12.522 --> 00:00:16.916
NARRATOR: Narration, visual directions,
citations, pronunciations, and accessibility

5
00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:20.212
NARRATOR: notes become visible before
production starts.

6
00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:25.112
NARRATOR: Each task is routed by capability
instead of being tied to one AI company.

7
00:00:25.112 --> 00:00:29.833
NARRATOR: Planning can use Claude, OpenAI,
Ollama, or another compatible bridge.

8
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:32.900
NARRATOR: Speech, transcription, images, and
video can also use

9
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.737
NARRATOR: approved local or hosted tools.

10
00:00:35.737 --> 00:00:38.200
NARRATOR: The project's data policy blocks
restricted information

11
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.826
NARRATOR: before it can reach a hosted
provider.

12
00:00:40.946 --> 00:00:45.192
NARRATOR: Fresh AI output may vary, even when
a provider accepts a seed.

13
00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:50.674
NARRATOR: The workflow therefore records every
accepted result, its checksum, model revision,

14
00:00:50.674 --> 00:00:52.045
NARRATOR: request, and provenance.

15
00:00:52.045 --> 00:00:56.108
NARRATOR: During frozen replay, model and
network calls are prohibited.

16
00:00:56.108 --> 00:01:01.253
NARRATOR: The system verifies and reuses the
exact bytes that reviewers already accepted.

17
00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.165
NARRATOR: Automation never becomes the release
authority.

18
00:01:04.165 --> 00:01:08.595
NARRATOR: A course pilot requires separate
approval of the script and evidence,

19
00:01:08.595 --> 00:01:10.639
NARRATOR: the visual treatment, and the
final master.

20
00:01:10.639 --> 00:01:15.205
NARRATOR: The resulting package includes
captions, transcripts, chapters, bibliography,

21
00:01:15.205 --> 00:01:21.294
NARRATOR: source coverage, asset credits, AI
disclosure, and quality reports—ready for

22
00:01:21.294 --> 00:01:23.831
NARRATOR: deliberate human review and manual
Panopto import.
